## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native SwiftUI parity of **`TeslaAccountSection`** at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TeslaAccountSection.*` — 11 files (10 Swift + a `.strings` catalog), following the repo's established multi-file surface architecture (Adapter / Model / Seams / View / Views / States / Previews + adapter & model test suites).

**Parity with the web source** (`features/settings/components/TeslaAccountSection.tsx`):
- All hooks bound through **shared P1/S8 seams** (status / action / toast / auth-expiry) — no HTTP in the view.
- **Every state renders**: loading, empty, error+retry, data (connected w/ "Expires in Nd" pill + "Token expires…" / not-connected / disconnected + reconnect body), plus the orthogonal stale/offline freshness axis.
- All web i18n keys via the **P1/S10 facade**; VoiceOver labels on every control; `view.opened` telemetry (P1/S11); the disconnect `ConfirmDialog` → native `.alert`; `useToast` → toast seam.

**In-scope verification — all GREEN:**
- `swiftformat --lint`: 0/10 • `swiftlint --strict`: 0 violations • check-placeholders: 0
- Clean compile in the **real iOS + macOS app targets** (0 errors in my files)
- **51 unit tests pass** (adapter + model status/actions + a11y + i18n), executed in an isolated SwiftPM harness under Swift 6 strict concurrency.

**Gate outcome: `EXIT=65 / STATUS=BLOCKED`** (logged at `.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p4-apple-feature-views-0216-TeslaAccountSection.log`). The full-app `xcodebuild build test` cannot return 0 because **293 pre-existing, committed, out-of-scope surfaces** don't compile against `Shared.xcframework` (e.g. a duplicate `ChargeSessionDTO` declaration in `dashboard-widgets`) plus a macOS widget signing requirement — none of which this prompt is permitted to modify. Per the Honesty Covenant I reported this as BLOCKED rather than fake a pass. I also built the KMP `Shared.xcframework` (a git-ignored prerequisite) so the gate was genuinely runnable. Committed the surface + honest log; no foreign file touched.

